<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaduna State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaduna State is a state of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, with its capital at Kaduna, the former administrative centre of colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-region-nigeria">Northern Nigeria</a>. It took its present name in 1976 and its present borders in 1987, when Katsina State was separated from it. It contains the historic city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaria">Zaria</a>, seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of Zazzau, and has a mixed Muslim and Christian population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaduna-state.jpg" alt="Kaduna State" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Derivative work: User:Profoss - Original work:Uwe Dedering · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigeria_-_Kaduna.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
